notes:
I found two free drop-in options for Halton Hills toddlers. Both come off the operators' own pages.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Kids & Me drop-in neighbourhood group, Halton Hills Public Library Acton Branch",
      "age_fit": "families with babies or children up to 6 years of age",
      "when": "Thursdays 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.; follows the school calendar, starting the second week of September, closed statutory holidays and the December/January break",
      "price": "free",
      "source_name": "Halton Region"
    },
    {
      "name": "EarlyON Child and Family Centres (Acton and Georgetown), Links2Care",
      "age_fit": "children from birth to their 6th birthday with a parent or caregiver",
      "price": "free",
      "source_name": "Links2Care"
    }
  ]
}
```

- **Kids & Me:** The Acton Thursday time is from Halton Region's parenting programs page. That page also lists Wednesday and Thursday sessions in Milton and Oakville, which aren't in Halton Hills. I didn't find a Georgetown time.
- **EarlyON:** Links2Care's page says it's free and runs drop-in, registered and online programs. The current schedule sits further down that page, and I couldn't read specific days or times. The only timetable I found was last summer's, so I left `when` out rather than guess.
- **Left out:** Halton Hills Gymnastics Centre has an under-4 drop-in on Tuesdays and Thursdays, but it costs $15, so it isn't free. The library's toddler storytimes came from a stale events page, so I left them out too.
